title:: CaosMIDITrackIn
summary:: MIDI keyboard input tap for one melodic track.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosMIDI, Classes/CaosTrack, Classes/CaosInstrument

description::
Listens to note on/off on one MIDI input and plays the current
link::Classes/CaosInstrument:: voice of a melodic track. The sequence is not
frozen: a key press triggers the voice, and the next sequencer step continues
with its own note line.

Monophonic with last-note priority: the most recent key sounds and, when it is
released, the previous held key sounds again. The audio mute/solo state of the
track applies, so a muted track does not sound from the keyboard. Velocity scales
the code::amp:: arguments of that note only; the instrument's stored parameters
are not modified.

If the track has a pending instrument (for example after re-evaluating
code::CaosGear.bass2:: with other parameters), the next note activates it. A key
that is already held keeps its old timbre through its sustain and release.

The melodic instruments use one-shot envelopes, so note off does not cut the
tail: every trigger creates a new voice and the envelope releases itself. For
sustained keyboard playing the SynthDefs would need gated envelopes.

code::install:: is separated from code::new:: so the note state machine can be
tested without MIDI hardware.

classmethods::

method:: new
code::
tap = CaosMIDITrackIn(track);
::

instancemethods::

method:: track
Read-only track being played.

method:: install
Connects the note-on and note-off link::Classes/MIDIdef:: responders to a source
uid and channel. code::channel:: can be nil for omni.
code::
tap.install(srcUID, 0);
::

method:: noteOn
method:: noteOff
MIDI entry points; they can also be called by tests without responders.
code::noteOn:: ignores the note when the track is not audible.

method:: releaseAll
Releases the sounding keyboard note and clears the held keys. Used by
code::CaosMIDI.panic:: and when detaching.

method:: free
Calls code::releaseAll:: and frees both responders.

method:: heldNotes
method:: sounding
Read-only monophonic state: the keys still held, in press order, and the note
currently sent to the voice (nil when nothing sounds from the keyboard).
